# @leooelx/plugin-scaffolder-environment-matrix-field

A dynamic Material UI React extension for the Backstage Scaffolder allowing users to inject environment-specific variables and secrets into Software Templates.

## Why this plugin?
The default Scaffolder UI lacks a robust structure for prompting users to input variables (like Database Connection Strings, Vault Secrets, or API Keys) that change depending on the CI/CD pipeline environment (e.g., DEV, HML, PRD).

This component solves this by providing a clean, dynamic matrix where developers can overwrite default values per environment, directly in the Backstage UI during template instantiation.

## Installation

```bash
yarn workspace app add @leooelx/plugin-scaffolder-environment-matrix-field
```

## Configuration

Register the custom field extension in your `packages/app/src/App.tsx`:

```tsx
import { environmentMatrixFieldExtension } from '@leooelx/plugin-scaffolder-environment-matrix-field';

const app = createApp({
  // ...
  components: {
    // ...
  },
  scaffolder: {
    customFieldExtensions: [environmentMatrixFieldExtension],
  },
});
```
